    "body": "The **DM Screen** tab in the Reliquary (**Compendium → Reliquary**, `/rules` → DM Screen) is a built-in, always-available quick-reference: the tables you'd otherwise keep on a physical screen at the table.\n\n## What's covered\n\nSwitch between five sections with the button row at the top, then between that section's reference tables underneath:\n\n- **Combat**: actions in combat, common bonus actions, common reactions, cover, conditions, death saving throws, creature size & space, object AC, object HP, underwater combat.\n- **Ability Checks**: skills by ability, difficulty class bands, common contests, carrying capacity, jumping.\n- **Environment**: light & vision, exhaustion, falling, travel pace, food & water, resting.\n- **Spellcasting**: spell slot levels by class level, concentration.\n- **Equipment & Services**: lifestyle expenses per day, food/drink/lodging, services, mounts, waterborne vehicles, donning & doffing armor.\n\nThis reference is static: it isn't affected by your campaign's custom rules and needs no setup. For house rules that override or extend the SRD, use the **Custom Rules** tab instead.\n\n## How do I...\n\n### Look up a rule in the middle of a fight\n\n1. Open **Compendium → Reliquary** in the sidebar. **DM Screen** is the first tab.\n2. Click the section you need: **Combat**, **Ability Checks**, **Environment**, **Spellcasting** or **Equipment & Services**.\n3. Scan the tables. On a wide screen they sit in two columns so you can read a name and its description side by side.\n\nFor example, for what a condition does, go to **Combat** and find **Conditions**. For a difficulty number, go to **Ability Checks** and find **Difficulty Class**. For how long a party can march in a day, go to **Environment** and find **Travel Pace**.\n\nYou can move between sections with the left and right arrow keys once one of the section buttons has focus.\n\n### Find the full text of a rule\n\nThe screen is a summary. For the complete wording, use the **Compendium** tab, which has the full rules text, and search it there.\n\n### Keep my own house rule on the screen\n\nThe screen is fixed and does not change with your campaign. To keep a house rule, write it on the **Custom Rules** tab. You can mark it visible to players, so it also appears in their rules reference.\n\n### Find out how a Grimoire feature works\n\nOpen the **DM Manual** tab, the manual you are reading. Pick a page from the list on the left, or type in the **Search manual…** box.\n\n## Searching the manual with a question\n\nThe search box matches words in page titles, summaries and text, so a short phrase such as \"hide NPC\" or \"fog\" finds pages directly.\n\nIf you type a whole question, such as \"how do I hide an NPC from the players\", and no page contains those exact words, Grimoire can suggest pages instead. Up to three appear under **Suggested pages**, best match first. A few things to know:\n\n- It tries this only once you have typed at least 8 characters and paused for a moment.\n- It needs AI switched on for the campaign. With AI off, nothing you type is sent anywhere, and you see **No matches.**\n- It costs you no credits.\n- Ordinary word search always wins: Suggested pages appears only when plain search finds nothing.\n\nOn a phone, the page list fills the screen until you open a page, and **All pages** takes you back to the list.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Reliquary: Overview](#reliquary-overview)\n- [Custom Rules (House Rules)](#custom-rules-house-rules)\n- [SRD Compendium](#srd-compendium)"
